60,3,1,talk,Mizuki,,"Candidate A, the Study Commons, fits the demand for general space and high user ratings perfectly.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Victoria,,"A is good, but B, the Media Center, is specialist space, which we know is often underused.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Benjamin,,"C, the Path Network, is a non-starter for me. Weather delays and outdoor work are too risky.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Kenji,,"D, the Lab Ventilation, involves mechanical plant. With costs rising 20%, that's a huge financial risk.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Shunichi,,"D is the only one that solves the technician's manual labor crisis. It's a necessity, not a luxury.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Mizuki,,"@Shunichi, I sympathize, but A serves the entire student body, not just a few technicians.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Victoria,,A conversion of a ground-floor hall might be less disruptive than a full lab overhaul.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Benjamin,,A is indoors and doesn't seem to rely on the volatile mechanical market as much as D.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Kenji,,I agree with Benjamin. A is a safer bet for the budget than the ventilation upgrade.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@Mizuki, if the labs aren't upgraded, the staff will burn out. That's a different kind of ""user"" failure.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Mizuki,,But the booking data shows general rooms are turned away all year. A solves a systemic problem.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Victoria,,I'm leaning toward A. It maximizes utility while minimizing the risk of off-site rental costs.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Benjamin,,A is the most likely to be delivered on time. I vote for the Study Commons.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Kenji,,I'll support A. It's the most fiscally responsible choice given the current tender trends.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Shunichi,,"I can't ignore the technicians, but I see the consensus. However, I still believe D is the most urgent.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Mizuki,,I'll vote for A. It's the best fit for the community.,"{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Victoria,,I'm with Mizuki. A it is.,"{""words"":6,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,pass,Benjamin,,Over,"{""forced"":false,""empty"":false}"
78,3,4,pass,Kenji,,Over,"{""forced"":false,""empty"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Shunichi,,I'll stick with D. The manual labor issue is too severe to ignore.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
